@startuml 05-submission-state
' =====================================================================
' Automated Code Feedback -- Submission Lifecycle
' Traces to: FR-18, FR-29, FR-30, FR-42, NFR-6
'
' All three runtime modules read and write submission.state. If they
' disagree about the legal transitions, the nightly job will either
' double-grade or silently skip students. This diagram is the contract.
' =====================================================================

title Submission Lifecycle -- submission.state

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

[*] --> DISCOVERED : Gradescope Adapter\nsees a submission id\nnot yet in the DB

DISCOVERED : Row exists, tests not yet recorded.
DISCOVERED : Set by the platform adapter or by
DISCOVERED : the autograder client's first POST.

DISCOVERED --> TESTS_RECORDED : Autograder Client posts\nfunctional test outcomes
DISCOVERED --> TESTING_FAILED : autograder errored\nor timed out

TESTS_RECORDED : test_outcome rows present for
TESTS_RECORDED : every active grading target.
TESTS_RECORDED : **This is the nightly job's work queue.**

TESTS_RECORDED --> GENERATING : Orchestrator claims the row\n(guard against two runs)
GENERATING --> FEEDBACK_GENERATED : all targets produced\nfeedback, one row selected
GENERATING --> FEEDBACK_FAILED : LLM call failed after retries

FEEDBACK_GENERATED : feedback rows exist with
FEEDBACK_GENERATED : is_selected set. Nothing has
FEEDBACK_GENERATED : reached the student yet.

FEEDBACK_GENERATED --> DELIVERY_REQUESTED : Adapter triggers\nGradescope regrade
DELIVERY_REQUESTED --> DELIVERED : Autograder Client acks\nthat results.json was written
DELIVERY_REQUESTED --> DELIVERY_FAILED : regrade never ran,\nor ack timed out

DELIVERED : Student can see the feedback.
DELIVERED : Terminal for this submission id.

DELIVERED --> [*]

TESTING_FAILED : attempt_count incremented.
FEEDBACK_FAILED : attempt_count incremented.
DELIVERY_FAILED : attempt_count incremented.

TESTING_FAILED --> DISCOVERED : next run,\nattempt_count < 3
FEEDBACK_FAILED --> TESTS_RECORDED : next run,\nattempt_count < 3
DELIVERY_FAILED --> FEEDBACK_GENERATED : next run,\nattempt_count < 3

TESTING_FAILED --> ABANDONED : attempt_count >= 3
FEEDBACK_FAILED --> ABANDONED : attempt_count >= 3
DELIVERY_FAILED --> ABANDONED : attempt_count >= 3

ABANDONED : Surfaced on the instructor
ABANDONED : dashboard for manual handling.
ABANDONED : Never retried automatically.

ABANDONED --> [*]

note right of GENERATING #FFF8DC
  **Why a separate GENERATING state.**
  Without it, two overlapping nightly runs
  both see TESTS_RECORDED and both bill you
  for the same LLM calls. Claiming the row
  by transitioning it, in a single UPDATE
  with a WHERE on the old state, makes the
  claim atomic.

  UPDATE submission
     SET state = 'GENERATING'
   WHERE id = ?
     AND state = 'TESTS_RECORDED'

  If it updates zero rows, another worker
  already has it. Skip.
end note

note as N2 #FFF8DC
  **Resubmission is out of scope in the SRS
  and needs a ruling.** Gradescope students can
  submit many times, each with its own
  submission id. As drawn, each id is an
  independent row and all of them get graded,
  which is correct but multiplies LLM cost by
  the number of attempts.

  Options: grade every attempt, grade only the
  active or latest attempt, or grade only the
  final attempt after the deadline. The cheapest
  and most common choice is latest-only, which
  needs an is_active flag on submission and a
  step that deactivates superseded attempts.
  Decide this before Student A's cost estimate
  means anything.
end note

@enduml
